# Enterprise GitOps Platform with AI-Powered Kubernetes Operations

## Project Overview

This project implements an end-to-end GitOps platform for a microservices application using GitHub Actions, Amazon EKS, ArgoCD, Datadog, and an AI-powered Kubernetes troubleshooting agent.

## Technologies Used

* GitHub Actions
* Docker
* Amazon EKS
* Kubernetes
* Helm
* ArgoCD
* Datadog
* Python
* OpenRouter / LLM Integration

## Task 1 - Continuous Integration

### Features Implemented

* Automated GitHub Actions workflow
* Source code checkout
* Dependency installation
* Application build
* Docker image build
* Docker image push to registry

### Commands Used

```bash
docker build -t <image-name> .
docker push <image-name>
```

## Task 2 - Amazon EKS

### Features Implemented

* EKS Cluster Creation
* Worker Node Configuration
* Namespace Configuration
* Kubernetes Access Configuration

### Commands Used

```bash
eksctl create cluster --name <cluster-name> --region <region>
kubectl get nodes
kubectl get pods -A
```

## Task 3 - GitOps with ArgoCD

### Features Implemented

* ArgoCD Installation
* Git Repository Synchronization
* Automated Application Deployment
* Rollback Capability

### Commands Used

```bash
kubectl create namespace argocd
helm install argocd ...
kubectl get applications -n argocd
```

## Task 4 - Datadog Observability

### Features Implemented

* Kubernetes Infrastructure Monitoring
* Application Monitoring
* Log Collection
* Dashboard Creation
* Alerting

### Alerts Created

* High CPU Alert
* Memory Alert
* Pod Failure Alert
* Application Availability Alert

### Dashboards Created

* EKS Infrastructure Dashboard
* Application Performance Dashboard
* Infrastructure Utilization Dashboard

## Task 5 - AI Troubleshooting Agent

### Features Implemented

* Kubernetes Log Collection
* Event Collection
* Failure Analysis
* Root Cause Identification
* Automated Remediation Suggestions

### Scenarios Tested

1. CrashLoopBackOff / Pod Restart
2. Application Latency
3. Deployment Failure

### Run

```bash
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY=<API_KEY>
python3 ai-agent.py
```

## Task 6 - AIOps Comparison

### Comparison Areas

* Traditional Monitoring
* AI-Assisted Troubleshooting
* Root Cause Analysis
* Incident Resolution

### Run

```bash
python3 aiops-comparison.py
```

## Screenshots

All screenshots are stored in the screenshots/ directory.

## Outcome

Successfully implemented a complete GitOps platform with CI/CD automation, Kubernetes deployment, observability, monitoring, alerting, and AI-assisted troubleshooting.
